00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
The Scariest House You Have Ever Seen!

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Home Alone: The Holiday Heist is a comedy, family, tv
movie film directed by Peter Hewitt.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
10-year-old Finn is terrified to learn his family is relocating from sunny
California to Maine in the scariest house he has ever seen!

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Convinced that his new house is haunted, Finn sets up a series of
elaborate traps to catch the “ghost” in action.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Left home alone with his sister while their parents are stranded across town, Finn’s traps
catch a new target – a group of thieves who have targeted Finn’s house.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Finn Baxter, played by Christian Martyn.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Alexis Baxter, played by Jodelle Ferland.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Sinclair, played by Malcolm McDowell.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Jessica, played by Debi Mazar.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Mr. Hughes, played by Eddie Steeples.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Curtis Baxter, played by Doug Murray.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Home Alone: The Holiday Heist is a 2012 American Christmas
comedy television film directed by Peter Hewitt.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
A standalone sequel to Home Alone 4 (2002), it is the fifth
installment in the Home Alone franchise.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It stars Christian Martyn, Jodelle Ferland, Malcolm
McDowell, Debi Mazar, and Eddie Steeples.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film was produced by Fox Television Studios and premiered on ABC Family on November 25, 2012,
during the network's annual Countdown to 25 Days of Christmas programming block.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
It is the second film after Home Alone 3 not to focus on the McCallister family.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The tone is lighthearted.
